    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_88b2733026fc999817366ef65175102b3b2a4aabe125d79b5ac071da53dafba0",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: the auxiliary function f built from xi and xi' is not zero at a simple xi zero, while a zero of multiplicity r survives with multiplicity r-1. Symmetry and Littlewood therefore make zeros of f control N(T)-N_d(T). Jensen reduces the problem to a mollified mean square; rewriting f through a linear differential polynomial Q and importing Conrey's optimized parameters with Q(0)=1 gives kappa_d>0.70. Interpretation: f removes exactly one layer of vanishing, turning excess multiplicity into a zero set accessible to averaged estimates. Boundary: the construction bounds a distinct-zero proportion; it neither locates zeros nor proves simplicity, and Q(0)=1 restricts the admissible optimization.",
